---
import Article from '../layouts/Article.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<Article
  title={`Privacy — ${SITE.name}`}
  heading="Privacy"
  kicker="Policy"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} handles the information you share with us: sparingly, confidentially, and without tracking cookies.`}
>
  <p>
    Discretion is a professional obligation for this firm, not a compliance exercise. This page describes what
    we collect through this website and what we do with it. It is written to be read.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Enquiry details you send us</strong> — through the project review form or by email: your name,
      contact details, and whatever you choose to tell us about your project.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Aggregate, cookie-free analytics.</strong> This site uses Plausible, which records page views
      without cookies and without collecting personal data or tracking you across sites. That is why there is
      no cookie banner here.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we do with it</h2>
  <p>
    Enquiry details are used to respond to you and, if an engagement follows, to run it. They are read by the
    principals, stored securely, and shared with no one outside the firm except specialists retained on your
    engagement — who are bound to the same confidentiality. We do not sell, rent, or trade any information.
    We add no one to a mailing list without their explicit request.
  </p>

  <h2>Client confidentiality</h2>
  <p>
    We do not publish client names, project locations, photographs, or identifying details without written
    permission. This applies to prospective clients too: the fact that you enquired is itself confidential.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention and your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Enquiry information that does not lead to an engagement is deleted on request, and otherwise not kept
    beyond its usefulness. You may ask at any time what we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to
    delete it: write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Third parties</h2>
  <p>
    Form submissions are processed by our hosting provider's form service for delivery to us. Analytics are
    processed by Plausible. Neither is permitted to use your information for their own purposes.
  </p>

  <p class="annotation not-prose mt-10">Last updated: August 2026.</p>
</Article>
